        "readable_text": "Content:\nA matrix is said to be idempotent, when multiplied by itself, yields itself.\n\nContent:\nFor example, the matrix\n\nContent:\n[MATH: [3|\u2212 6; 1|\u2212 2]]\n\nContent:\nis idempotent because [MATH: B^2 = B]:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: B^{2}|= [3|\u2212 6; 1|\u2212 2][3|\u2212 6; 1|\u2212 2]; = [3 \u22c5 3 + (\u2212 6) \u22c5 1|3 \u22c5 (\u2212 6) + (\u2212 6) \u22c5 (\u2212 2); 1 \u22c5 3 + (\u2212 2) \u22c5 1|1 \u22c5 (\u2212 6) + (\u2212 2) \u22c5 (\u2212 2)]; = [3|\u2212 6; 1|\u2212 2]; = B]"
