      {
        "lesson_index": 6,
        "step_index": 4,
        "item_type": "step",
        "step_type": "example",
        "step_id": "16203",
        "content_id": "4416",
        "dom_id": "step-16203",
        "selector": "#step-16203",
        "step_anchor": "step-6",
        "title": "Finding a Power of an Idempotent Matrix",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Find <span class=\"math\">[MATH: C^5]</span> given that\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: [(1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2); 0|1|0; (1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2)]]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Find [MATH: C^5] given that\n[MATH: [(1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2); 0|1|0; (1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2)]]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we compute <span class=\"math\">[MATH: C^2]</span> as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: C^{2}|= C \u22c5 C; = [(1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2); 0|1|0; (1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2)] \u22c5 [(1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2); 0|1|0; (1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2)]; = [(1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2); 0|1|0; (1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2)]; = C]</span></p><p>Notice that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: C^2=C,]</span> so <span class=\"math\">[MATH: C]</span> is an idempotent matrix. </p><p>We can use this fact to compute <span class=\"math\">[MATH: C^5]</span> quickly, as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: C^{5}|= C^{2} \u22c5 C^{2} \u22c5 C; = C \u22c5 C \u22c5 C; = C^{2} \u22c5 C; = C \u22c5 C; = C^{2}; = C]</span></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: [(1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2); 0|1|0; (1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2)]]</span></p>",
