        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nFind [MATH: C^5] given that\n[MATH: [(1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2); 0|1|0; (1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2)]]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we compute [MATH: C^2] as follows:\n\n[MATH: C^{2}|= C \u22c5 C; = [(1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2); 0|1|0; (1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2)] \u22c5 [(1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2); 0|1|0; (1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2)]; = [(1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2); 0|1|0; (1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2)]; = C]\n\nNotice that [MATH: C^2=C,] so [MATH: C] is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute [MATH: C^5] quickly, as follows:\n\n[MATH: C^{5}|= C^{2} \u22c5 C^{2} \u22c5 C; = C \u22c5 C \u22c5 C; = C^{2} \u22c5 C; = C \u22c5 C; = C^{2}; = C]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: [(1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2); 0|1|0; (1)/(2)|0|(1)/(2)]]"
